WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.535
-Tonight was the second
Democratic debate,

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.569
or, as nine candidates
called it,

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:06.906
"Operation Destroy Joe Biden."

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.875
Everybody went after Biden,
but he said,

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:11.344
with 10 people onstage,
it was less of a debate

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.879
and more of like
a lightning round

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:18.151
Or, in Bernie Sanders' case,
a struck-by-lightning round.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.986
Hey, you got to respect
a guy who combs his

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:20.986
hair with a balloon.

00:00:20.986 --> 00:00:23.189
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.157
Then he floats away like
the old man from "Up."

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:26.625
It's amazing.

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:28.360
But it was a big night,
and, in the end, a lot of people

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.696
thought Kamala Harris
won the be debate.

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:32.065
She had what was probably --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:36.603
Yeah. She had what was probably
the line of the night.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.838
At one point, all the candidates
were talking over each other,

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.874
and that's when she stepped in
and dropped the hammer.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.041
Watch this.

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:45.612
-Part of the issue of --
Hey, guys, you know what?

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.447
America does not want to
witness a food fight.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.614
They want to
know how we're going to

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:51.483
put food on their table.

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:54.687
-Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.389
She was so good,
Trump endorsed Biden

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.590
so that he wouldn't
have to face her.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.426
It's like, "Yeah, he's great."

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:02.661
Tonight, we got to see Bernie
and Biden onstage together.

00:01:02.661 --> 00:01:04.530
Yeah, here they are right there.
Yeah.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:09.902
It looks like they're debating
Viagra versus Cialis.

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:12.572
Look, I'm not saying those two
are old, but their podiums

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:18.178
were the only ones with tennis
balls the bottom.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.713
But get this -- there was
a 40-year age difference

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:24.350
between tonight's candidates,
ranging from 37 to 77.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.719
With Pete Buttigieg next to
Biden, it looked like

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:30.223
Take Your Kid to Work Day.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.325
Speaking of Buttigieg,
he said Democrats need to

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.527
move the party forward
and claimed his opponents

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.796
want to return to the 1990s.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.464
Hey, Pete, the top movies
right now are

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.466
"Toy Story," "Men in Black,"
and "Aladdin."

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:42.135
We're already back in the '90s.

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:48.174
Sorry to say.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.043
Well, in addition to
the front-runners,

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:52.344
we also got to know
some of the underdogs,

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:54.413
and, early on, a lot of people
noticed that one of them,

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:56.248
Andrew Yang,
wasn't wearing a tie.

00:01:56.248 --> 00:01:57.983
Take a look at this. Yeah.

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.552
When he realized you
can go casual,

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.853
Biden tried to take off
his pants,

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:04.057
and you go, "No, hey,
you can't do that."

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.925
Finally, you guys,
so much happened during

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.927
the two nights of the debate,
it's hard to cover it all.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.896
so I was thinking we
could ask Tariq

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:12.431
for a debate rap recap.

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:15.067
I mean...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:18.805
I know the second debate just
ended 30 minutes ago,

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.473
but, Tariq,
what do you think, bud?

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.342
-I think we could pull that off.
-All right. Let's do this.

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:26.846
Roots, hit it.
♪♪

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:36.489
♪ They were, unh ♪
♪ They were, unh ♪

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:37.823
